<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Workspaces (中文)</title><link>https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/</link><description>探索激发生产力的工作空间。</description><language>zh-CN</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:27:04 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>马克西姆·赫克尔</title><link>https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/534-maxime-heckel</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://maximeheckel.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Maxime Heckel&lt;/a&gt; is a software engineer originally from France, now based in New York City. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He is currently working as a product engineer at Linear.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In his spare time, he loves to tinker with frontend development, WebGL/WebGPU, shaders, and graphics programming at large. This area of computer science is an endless source of knowledge and he has spent the past 5 years learning as much as possible.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He’s documenting all of these learnings and distilling them into experiments and essays that he wished existed when he was getting started on his blog which is also his longest ongoing side project (8 years this year).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Twitter (X) → &lt;a href="https://x.com/MaximeHeckel?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;x.com/MaximeHeckel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;GitHub → &lt;a href="https://github.com/maximeheckel?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;github.com/maximeheckel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Blog → &lt;a href="https://blog.maximeheckel.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;blog.maximeheckel.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/51290c69-a48a-4a66-b279-b1841120bb59/Maxime_Heckel_4.jpg?t=1782561893"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/b2c38fec-b6e2-4d6e-a891-318c70d1c677/Maxime_Heckel_2.jpg?t=1782561918"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/edfbb91b-5786-4fa8-a22c-482532a45b36/Maxime_Heckel_9.jpg?t=1782561983"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/6a93ab2b-14db-45af-b2a7-a0ef439d4b3c/Maxime_Heckel_8.jpg?t=1782562008"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/a5a7f174-c050-44d4-9232-38edc0d732b6/Maxime_Heckel_5.jpg?t=1782562033"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/71812809-cdd9-4c83-96f1-82df035cf444/Maxime_Heckel_1.jpg?t=1782562063"/&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What items are in your workspace?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Display: 27" Apple Studio Display from 2022&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;MacBook Pro M4 Max 36GB of memory (Silver)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monitor arm: &lt;a href="https://store.hermanmiller.com/home-desk-accessories/jarvis-single-monitor-arm/2548325.html?lang=en_US&amp;amp;utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Jarvis Monitor Arm from Fully&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Desk Mat: Wool Felt Desk Pad from Grovemade (light gray)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Keyboard: &lt;a href="https://modedesigns.com/products/sixtyfive?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Mode SixtyFive (2024), with copper accent color&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mouse: &lt;a href="https://amzn.to/4g3W0fD?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;MX Master 3 &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;TrackPad: &lt;a href="https://amzn.to/4wd84zN?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Apple Magic Trackpad (USB-C)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.apple.com/airpods-pro/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;AirPods Pro 3&lt;/a&gt; as my daily driver at my desk or on the go&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apple wired earbuds USB-C when I need high mic quality&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lamp: &lt;a href="https://www.mi.com/global/product/mi-led-desk-lamp-1s/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Xiaomi Mi Home Smart Led Desk Lamp&lt;/a&gt; (I don't think you can buy it anymore)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pencil Case: &lt;a href="https://amzn.to/4beLDSO?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Muji Polypropylene Pen Case&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Books&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://fleuret.org/francois/lbdl.html?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;The Little Book of Deep Learning&lt;/a&gt; by Francois Fleuret&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://amzn.to/3R1EbDP?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;The Shape of Design&lt;/a&gt; by Frank Chimero&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://buddybindery.com/products/bootstrapping-computing?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Bootstrapping Computing&lt;/a&gt; by Alexander D. Obenauer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;(I'm not a huge fan of "tech books" despite working in tech, but these are 3 books I really enjoyed and that coincidentally fit my desk aesthetic quite well)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What software do you find yourself using on a regular basis?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://arc.net/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Arc browser&lt;/a&gt; (at this point you'd have to take this from my cold dead hands)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.raycast.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Raycast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://mymind.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;MyMind&lt;/a&gt; to save inspiration&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://cursor.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Cursor&lt;/a&gt; as my main editor (I still write code by hand)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://openai.com/codex/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Codex&lt;/a&gt; (when I do not feel to write code by hand)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://ghostty.org/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Ghostty&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://linear.app/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Linear&lt;/a&gt; (even outside of work)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apple Notes (this is my source of truth for everything, I store and sort inspiration for upcoming projects and topic ideas for blog posts). I like having these available offline and automatically synced across all devices without having to think about it. I trust Apple with my notes although I did set up some scripts to back them up in markdown on a monthly basis "just in case" and also to try out other note taking apps&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://superwhisper.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Superwhisper&lt;/a&gt; (when I feel to talk to my computer instead of typing)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What is the most recent item that you've added to your workspace?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's my &lt;a href="https://modedesigns.com/products/sixtyfive?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Mode 65 keyboard&lt;/a&gt;, which I got back in 2024. I missed the first gen Mode 65 and was pretty sad about it so the moment they released the second version of it, I jumped on it and immediately bought it. It's my first mechanical keyboard. I picked this one for its:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;compact form factor&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;material used: it feels heavy and premium, it's all aluminium&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;I opted for a Copper accent to add a subtle pop of color to the desk&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What is one change you'd like to make to your current workspace?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;My biggest regret is opting for the VESA-mounted Studio Display instead of the one with the adjustable mount. My girlfriend has it, and it feels so much better to adjust than my monitor arm. Since this display now has a second generation version, I may get tempted to upgrade it and finally scratch that itch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another small detail concerns my laptop stands, ideally, I'd have them hidden behind my monitor to keep the desk surface clear since it's pretty small. I've seen several people 3D print custom mounts for their MacBooks, but I haven't attempted that yet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Walk us through your morning routine—what’s the first thing you do at your desk?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;First thing is bringing in my small tray with a nice pour over coffee and a quick breakfast (I know eating at one's desk is not a good habit, but I still do it)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;While eating and drinking coffee, I catch up on everything work-related: Pull Request reviews from my European coworkers that happened overnight, newly filed issues, etc. I always dread this part because you can quickly get flooded with information first thing in the morning, which is why I pair it with coffee to make it a bit more enjoyable. I try to get it out of the way as soon as possible so I can organize my day quickly&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What’s one productivity trick that actually works for you?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;I have many side projects going on, including my blog and shader-related work. It can feel overwhelming, especially when learning about a brand new topic. I always try to chip away at my task list a little bit daily, for at least 1 hour. The daily goal is always very reachable and doesn't necessitate all this time. In general, once I complete it, I get into the flow and continue working through my project, often pushing further than anticipated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another trick is to keep my desk neat and clean after work; I rarely let it get out of control. I'm more willing to sit down and work there if it's orderly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What’s the most underrated app or tool you use every day?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Not underrated at this point but &lt;a href="https://raycast.com?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Raycast&lt;/a&gt; is the app I interact the most with (besides Linear of course). Here are my favorite extensions:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Window Management: I have keybindings to move my windows around very easily and cycle through different sizes, this lets me keep my desktop environment&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apple Reminders: Basically pilot everything in Apple Reminders from Raycast to set quick reminders, or reminders using natural language&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Download Video X/Twitter: Any work shared that I wish to consult later ends up in my personal offline archive (I just don't trust anyone to keep their account alive anymore, so I archive a lot of designs, URLs, and in this case videos featuring shaders, animations, etc)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quick Links: I have quick links to open my editor for each project and to access their custom URLs, all directly from Raycast&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also, a quick shoutout to &lt;a href="https://mymind.com?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=maxime-heckel" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;MyMind&lt;/a&gt; which is the second app I use the most. It's perhaps the most thoughtfully built app I've gotten to use &lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/powered-by?publication_logo=https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.beehiiv.com%2Fcdn-cgi%2Fimage%2Ffit%3Dscale-down%2Cformat%3Dauto%2Conerror%3Dredirect%2Cquality%3D80%2Fuploads%2Fpublication%2Flogo%2F9e0ab799-69a2-448f-b9a1-c03f8f3356e9%2FLogo_2.png%3Fv%3D1788837752&amp;amp;publication_name=Workspaces&amp;amp;utm_campaign=cd11bcb7-065f-4b3f-be2d-af27de46a7e4&amp;amp;utm_medium=post_rss&amp;amp;utm_source=workspaces" target="_blank"&gt;Powered by beehiiv&lt;/a&gt;</description><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:27:04 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>罗天成</title><link>https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/533-tiancheng-luo</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Tiancheng Luo（又名 bbbigdear）是一位产品设计师和科技与生活方式类创作者，专注于工作空间美学、现代生活方式以及精心设计的科技产品。他通过富有电影感的叙事方式和对产品的亲身探索，分享那些将功能性与视觉设计融为一体的工具与物件。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Instagram → &lt;a href="https://www.instagram.com/bbbigdeer/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;instagram.com/bbbigdeer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Threads → &lt;a href="https://www.threads.com/@bbbigdeer?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;threads.com/@bbbigdeer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;TikTok → &lt;a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@bbbigdeer?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;tiktok.com/@bbbigdeer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;YouTube → &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/@bigdeeer?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;youtube.com/@bigdeeer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/6c438768-b421-4d9b-87d8-065b787f5105/DSC00691.jpg?t=1781356253"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/d26029e6-c1a3-4cd5-8f65-f84e086d7bc6/DSC00650.jpg?t=1781356353"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/1b47e11a-2c6a-4f09-aa37-1de07bdb25bb/DSC00709.jpg?t=1781356371"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/f083ab73-6412-4ead-a530-716902177120/DSC00642.jpg?t=1781356383"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/2ce43d6a-bdbb-49ef-8d63-a4fd0ebe7a26/DSC00721.jpg?t=1781356406"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/fa4bc797-bcf0-4f10-a8ba-25aded6d6fe2/DSC00786.jpg?t=1781356421"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/433084ce-c5c0-427f-a4c0-47ff009ea4e9/DSC00747.jpg?t=1781356434"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/a9cf57db-ccf6-40a5-930d-db8c98101a7b/DSC00761.jpg?t=1781356447"/&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你的工作空间里有哪些主要物品？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://workspacesxyz.link/LShaped?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Vernal L 形升降桌&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apple Studio Display&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apple Mac Mini&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://amzn.to/3QeShkY?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Lofree Touch 鼠标&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://amzn.to/3QmgoOC?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Harman Kardon Aura Studio 音箱&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://amzn.to/4aqVbtC?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Bambu Lab A1 3D 打印机&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;分体式人体工学机械键盘&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你最近为工作空间添置了什么物品？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;最近添置的是来自 Vernal 的 &lt;a href="https://workspacesxyz.link/LShaped?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tiancheng-luo" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;L 形升降桌&lt;/a&gt;。它彻底改变了整个工作区的氛围，给了我更多空间去区分不同类型的工作，也让整个环境显得更有条理。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你希望对目前的工作空间做出哪一项改变？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我希望工作空间能更宁静、更有设计上的巧思。不只是桌面，而是更立体的整体空间。目前我觉得墙面区域还需要更用心地去设计，让整个环境显得更统一、更有秩序。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;跟我们聊聊你的晨间例行流程——坐到办公桌前你做的第一件事是什么？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;打开音箱。我做的第一件事永远是打开音箱。音乐会帮助我自然而然地进入工作状态。之后，我通常会查看消息、梳理当天的想法，然后慢慢进入拍摄或写脚本的节奏。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;哪一条效率技巧对你真的有效？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我觉得每个人都应该最终建立起自己独特的工作流程，而不是试图去复刻别人的。目前，AI 大约占了我工作室工作流程的 30%，所以学会如何与 AI 工具协作对我来说已经变得非常重要。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你每天都会使用的最被低估的应用或工具是什么？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;ChatGPT。我觉得每个人的 ChatGPT 都会随着时间变得与众不同。经过几个月的对话，它开始更深层次地理解你。对我来说，它已经不再只是一个工具，而是一个能帮我整理思路、打磨想法、并挑战我思维方式的存在。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/powered-by?publication_logo=https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.beehiiv.com%2Fcdn-cgi%2Fimage%2Ffit%3Dscale-down%2Cformat%3Dauto%2Conerror%3Dredirect%2Cquality%3D80%2Fuploads%2Fpublication%2Flogo%2F9e0ab799-69a2-448f-b9a1-c03f8f3356e9%2FLogo_2.png%3Fv%3D1788837752&amp;amp;publication_name=Workspaces&amp;amp;utm_campaign=ab3ba0e7-f734-4297-959d-c056ba0949b7&amp;amp;utm_medium=post_rss&amp;amp;utm_source=workspaces" target="_blank"&gt;由 beehiiv 提供支持&lt;/a&gt;</description><pubDate>Sat, 13 Jun 2026 13:52:51 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Jack Zerby</title><link>https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/240-jack-zerby</link><description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/83ffefc4-12e8-4eba-83aa-2833cea00251/Jack_Zerby_thumbnail.png?t=1781142493"/&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jackzerby.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Jack Zerby&lt;/a&gt; 目前是 &lt;a href="http://gumroad.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Gumroad&lt;/a&gt; 的设计主管，也是 &lt;a href="http://dogma.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Dogma&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="http://designfordecks.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Design For Decks&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="http://biddyhq.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Biddy&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="http://getdohq.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;DOHQ&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://Flavors.me?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Flavors.me&lt;/a&gt; 和 &lt;a href="https://www.businessinsider.com/what-is-goodsie-2011-5?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Goodsie&lt;/a&gt; 的创始人。&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;他曾为 &lt;a href="https://vimeo.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Vimeo&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://pentagram.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Pentagram&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://frogdesign.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Frog&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://rga.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;R/GA&lt;/a&gt; 等公司工作，并为 &lt;a href="https://teachable.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Teachable&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://americanexpress.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Amex&lt;/a&gt; 和 &lt;a href="https://staked.us/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Staked&lt;/a&gt; 等公司提供咨询。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Twitter → &lt;a href="https://twitter.com/jackzerby?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;twitter.com/jackzerby&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/82cc4dc3-638a-4519-812b-2f7d886e502a/image.png?t=1781142289"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/b0d3e3c1-2144-499a-9c87-dfa47ed0db9e/image.png?t=1781142303"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/f52ad4d3-6db1-43f2-8909-43f7de552298/image.png?t=1781142317"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/10e73223-99ca-43d5-bc5c-47dc9abef0f8/image.png?t=1781142331"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/bf263210-a906-497a-b49e-a224b5da2dc0/image.png?t=1781142346"/&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/57f0439f-b599-4d90-8837-1a2823061f7d/image.png?t=1781142360"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;杰克的妻子最近重新设计了他的工作空间，变成你今天看到的这个样子。 &lt;a href="https://alovelyliving.com/office-update-featuring-ben-moore-caldwell-green/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby#/" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;你可以（而且应该！）在这里查看更多重新设计背后的照片和想法！&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你的工作空间中包含哪些设备？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;绿色 iMac M1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;MAudio Keystation 61键 MIDI 钢琴&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;EV RE20 播客麦克风&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pottery Barn Pittsburgh 站立式办公桌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://diycandy.com/diy-industrial-pipe-shelving/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-zerby" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;DIY 黑色管道置物架&lt;/a&gt;‍&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;琴叶榕盆栽&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Jan 2023 06:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>杰克·雷恩斯</title><link>https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/252-jack-raines</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://twitter.com/Jack_Raines?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-raines" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Jack Raines&lt;/a&gt; 是一个名为 Young Money 的金融博客的作者，每周有 31,000 人阅读该博客两次。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;他还负责编辑 Litquidity 的每日金融通讯 &lt;a href="https://www.execsum.co/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-raines" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Exec Sum&lt;/a&gt;。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;在 Columbia Business School 攻读 MBA 期间，他同时完成了以上所有工作。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;有趣的事实：他曾被挪威驱逐出境，在阿根廷学会了萨尔萨舞，还差点因为一篇 &lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jackraines/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-raines" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;讽刺性的 LinkedIn 帖子&lt;/a&gt; 被商学院开除。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/2fbcbb73-0bf8-4377-a108-4ac404a2b846/image.png?t=1781141970"/&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你的工作空间里有哪些设备？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;MacBook Pro&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.thexebec.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=jack-raines" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Xebec（附带的双显示器）&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;蓝牙鼠标&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;日记本（算不上工作空间的一部分，但总是在我的包里）&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你最喜欢的工作空间物品是什么？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我的 Xebec。它便于携带，还能把我的屏幕扩展成三倍大小。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你是如何激发创造力的？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我从未主动激发过创造力，都是创造力来找我。创造力通常在我去健身房、坐地铁，或凌晨 1 点泡在小酒吧时迸发出来。灵感来袭时，我会给自己发几条片段，等回到电脑前再回看。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你是如何管理工作与生活平衡的？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;管理工作与生活平衡的最好方式，就是去做那些你根本不需要刻意平衡的事情。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你典型的写作流程是怎样的？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我坐下来，先写 15 分钟，然后上 Twitter 找一条想引用的推文，在 Twitter 上拖延 20 分钟，把手机扔到床上，关掉 Twitter，再继续埋头写通讯。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/powered-by?publication_logo=https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.beehiiv.com%2Fcdn-cgi%2Fimage%2Ffit%3Dscale-down%2Cformat%3Dauto%2Conerror%3Dredirect%2Cquality%3D80%2Fuploads%2Fpublication%2Flogo%2F9e0ab799-69a2-448f-b9a1-c03f8f3356e9%2FLogo_2.png%3Fv%3D1788837752&amp;amp;publication_name=Workspaces&amp;amp;utm_campaign=9f5948bf-7675-461c-a892-8a62fe13d825&amp;amp;utm_medium=post_rss&amp;amp;utm_source=workspaces" target="_blank"&gt;由 beehiiv 提供技术支持&lt;/a&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 08 Feb 2023 06:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>大卫·海涅迈尔·汉森</title><link>https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/253-david-heinemeier-hansson</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://dhh.dk?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;David Heinemeier Hansson&lt;/a&gt;，也就是DHH，不需要正式介绍。但我们还是准备介绍一下。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;他是&lt;a href="https://rubyonrails.org/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Ruby on Rails&lt;/a&gt;的创造者，这个开源框架已被数十万开发者使用。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;他是&lt;a href="https://basecamp.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;Basecamp&lt;/a&gt;和&lt;a href="https://www.hey.com/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;HEY&lt;/a&gt;的联合创始人。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;他是一位畅销书作家，与联合创始人Jason Fried合著了四本书（&lt;a href="https://37signals.com/books/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson#rework" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;《重来》&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://37signals.com/books/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson#calm" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;《工作何必疯狂》&lt;/a&gt;、&lt;a href="https://37signals.com/books/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson#remote" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;《重来2：更为简单高效的远程工作方式》&lt;/a&gt;，以及&lt;a href="https://37signals.com/books/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson#getting-real" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;《务实之道》&lt;/a&gt;。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;如果这些还不够，他还是FIA世界耐力锦标赛的&lt;a href="https://dhh.dk/?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson#driver" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;赛车手&lt;/a&gt;。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Twitter → &lt;a href="https://twitter.com/dhh?utm_source=workspaces.beehiiv.com&amp;amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;amp;utm_campaign=david-heinemeier-hansson" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank"&gt;twitter.com/dhh&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;img alt="" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/269219fe-657a-455e-9fce-87aaafb183ec/image.png?t=1781141694"/&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你的一天通常是什么样的？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;早上的时间用来送孩子上学。我通常在8:30左右坐下来开始工作。然后一般花一个小时左右处理邮件、报告之类的事情。接下来，最美好的日子就是从那时起完全自由，可以一头扎进有趣且有挑战性的项目中，最好是编程或写作。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你认为2023年远程工作的主要好处是什么？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我已经远程工作二十年了，对我来说好处始终如一。可以自由选择居住地，可以在家庭办公室工作，享受完全宁静以便专注，还能享受白天就在家人隔壁的灵活性。用什么都别想让我放弃这种生活。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;你是如何在多个进行中的项目之间平衡工作的？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我试着按季节来工作。有些季节专注于编程，有些用来写作，还有些则专注于业务本身。多任务处理是一个幻象。人类能做的只有瞎折腾。所以一次只保持一个主要项目在手，才是快速前进的关键。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/powered-by?publication_logo=https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.beehiiv.com%2Fcdn-cgi%2Fimage%2Ffit%3Dscale-down%2Cformat%3Dauto%2Conerror%3Dredirect%2Cquality%3D80%2Fuploads%2Fpublication%2Flogo%2F9e0ab799-69a2-448f-b9a1-c03f8f3356e9%2FLogo_2.png%3Fv%3D1788837752&amp;amp;publication_name=Workspaces&amp;amp;utm_campaign=83a7dc4d-a69e-4e2c-9009-696c7bc81e7e&amp;amp;utm_medium=post_rss&amp;amp;utm_source=workspaces" target="_blank"&gt;Powered by beehiiv&lt;/a&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 09 Feb 2023 06:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item></channel></rss>